   $q$Which choice best tells what happens in the poem, in order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker plants a bean, almost gives up, waits as Grandma says, and it sprouts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A bean sprouts, then the speaker plants it, then Grandma waters it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-order"},{"text":"The speaker plants a bean and checks it, and it never grows at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The speaker plants a bean, digs it up on Wednesday, and plants a new one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker plants a bean, almost gives up, waits as Grandma says, and it sprouts.$q$, $q$The poem moves from planting, to wanting to dig it out, to waiting, to the sprout on Saturday. The speaker never actually digs the seed up.$q$, 'draft', '0f4c9a89-f31b-5844-b0a7-bef9623cf1ce')
