   $q$What is the message of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rain is always better than sunshine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"When plans change, you can still find a way to have fun.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Flashlight tag is the best indoor game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-lesson"},{"text":"Picnics should never be planned for Saturdays.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When plans change, you can still find a way to have fun.$q$, $q$The rain ruins the park plan, but the speaker and Dad have an indoor picnic, and the poem says, "A day can change and still be good." The poem never says rain is better than sunshine.$q$, 'draft', '45e8d202-b39c-500e-a702-bdbe2cec142c')
