   $q$What is the lesson of this fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Young animals should never follow butterflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-lesson"},{"text":"Owls know every path in the jungle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Bright feathers make you the smartest animal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Listening carefully can help more than talking a lot.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Listening carefully can help more than talking a lot.$q$, $q$Parrot's talking confuses Monkey, but Owl listens and finds the way, then says, "I only listened." Owl even says, "I did not know," so Owl does not know every path.$q$, 'draft', '7b31b983-d958-5e59-99f3-f5eeb4f6a8ef')
